Subject: [PATCH] Recover a pending test-process exit status

Private test-runner fix for the PHP 8.3.35 OOM candidate.
Embargoed: Keep this patch private until disclosure.

The test runner checks process status without waiting after pipe EOF.
Wait using proc_close() before formatting termination status, and use
its exit code if the initial status still reports a running process.
The test and its required Termsig=9 expectation are unchanged.
No production PHP runtime code is changed by this patch.

diff --git a/run-tests.php b/run-tests.php
--- a/run-tests.php
+++ b/run-tests.php
@@ -1259,6 +1259,12 @@
     }
 
     $stat = proc_get_status($proc);
+    $finalExitcode = proc_close($proc);
+
+    // Pipe EOF may precede availability of the child's exit status.
+    if ($stat['running'] && $finalExitcode >= 0) {
+        $stat['exitcode'] = $finalExitcode;
+    }
 
     if ($stat['signaled']) {
         $data .= "\nTermsig=" . $stat['stopsig'] . "\n";
@@ -1270,7 +1276,6 @@
         $data .= "\nTermsig=" . $stat["exitcode"] . "\n";
     }
 
-    proc_close($proc);
     return $data;
 }
 
